# Echo Model SHA256 Checksum Manifest (R-4.2 reproducible delivery)
#
# Format: <sha256>  <filename>
#
# This manifest is generated by `bash Scripts/prepare_models.sh --generate-checksums`.
# After downloading models, run that command to populate the real checksum values;
# thereafter `prepare_models.sh` in download/verify mode compares each downloaded
# file's SHA256 and fails on mismatch.
#
# NOTE: Before committing, populate this file with the real models' SHA256 values
# (currently a placeholder structure). To generate:
#   1. bash Scripts/prepare_models.sh --generate-checksums
#   2. Confirm this file now contains 64-hex-digit checksum values
#   3. git add Scripts/model_checksums.sha256 && git commit
#
# Expected entries (filename must match prepare_models.sh exactly):
#   Manifest.json              (multilingual-e5-small mlpackage manifest)
#   whisper-tiny-q5_1.gguf     (Whisper ASR GGUF, R-5.4 tiny)
#   model.safetensors          (SigLIP2-B/32 checkpoint)
